{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ROUND 10: BLOCK, and the finding count went UP (7+ blocking, vs 1 in round 9). That reverses the\ntrend and is itself the signal — applying handoff #4's lesson 3: WHEN A PLAN KEEPS RETURNING\nDOUBLE-DIGIT FINDINGS, SUSPECT STRUCTURE, NOT WORDING. J9 blocked 8 times in this epic and splitting\nit into J10 produced a first-try PASS.\n\nMY RECOMMENDATION TO WHOEVER PICKS THIS UP: **SPLIT THIS TICKET IN TWO before spending round 11.**\nThis plan is carrying two independent changes, which is why every round finds new surface:\n\n  S1 — EXTRACT the retry/error cluster from `transport.py` into `adapters/jira_datacenter/retry.py`.\n       Pure, behaviour-preserving relocation forced by the LOCKED 800-LOC cap. Includes\n       `TlsVerificationError` (or `_tls_verification_error` at `:218` creates a circular import) and\n       re-exports so `test_jira_dc_config_settings.py:183-184` pass UNEDITED. Verifiable by a diff\n       read and two `wc -l`. Depends on 9263.\n\n  S2 — ADD the 429 policy in the extracted module: reuse `_errors.parse_retry_after` /\n       `MAX_BACKOFF_S`, jitter-then-clamp, and the per-CALL read/mutation opt-in.\n\nThe rounds show exactly why they should not ship together: rounds 1, 4, 8, 9 and 10 were all about\nS2's POLICY (reuse, duplicate-risk scoping, citation precision, per-call boundary, cap-exhaustion\nbehaviour), while rounds 6-7 were about S1's MECHANICS (what moves, what routes through what, which\ntree the LOC is measured on). Each round the two interleave and a fix to one re-opens surface in the\nother. Split, and S1 becomes a one-pass mechanical review.\n\nROUND 10'S FINDINGS, for whoever continues (verify each against `origin/main`, not your branch):\n 1. [G6, GENUINELY IMPORTANT AND UNANSWERED] The plan never says WHAT EXCEPTION ESCAPES when the\n    429 retry cap is exhausted. Re-raising the raw `JIRAError` would leak a vendor type straight\n    past the adapter boundary that `_as_backend_http_error` exists to seal — callers catch\n    `BackendHTTPError`. This is a real design hole, not wording, and it is the single best argument\n    that S2 deserves its own focused review.\n 2. [G6] HOW `_paged_search` opts in is ambiguous: does it always pass `rate_limit_retry=True`, or\n    accept and forward a flag from its callers? Opposite failure modes.\n 3. [E4] Whether `_paged_search` routes through `_call_logged` is asserted from 9263's PLAN TEXT,\n    not from landed code — because 9263 is not on main yet. Re-verify once 1129 lands.\n 4. [COH] Scope says \"ELEVEN read call sites\"; the table has TEN rows. My own arithmetic error.\n 5. [G1G2] The mutation AC uses an ellipsis (\"create_issue, add_comment, add_label, …\") where the\n    transport has ~10 distinct non-opting mutation sites; enumerate them rather than gesture.\n\nDO NOT treat 1, 2 and 5 as wording fixes. 1 in particular changes what the code does."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785543467431401001,"uuid":"0f0ff3e7-44d3-4a5c-b48f-73d1c9ac3f0f"}